## 12.1 Architecture

Use a clear, maintainable structure with reusable components.

Suggested organization:

- `app/` — application setup and routing.
- `components/ui/` — reusable design-system components.
- `components/layout/` — headers, sidebars, navigation, footers.
- `components/profile/` — profile cards and profile sections.
- `components/forms/` — reusable field and form components.
- `components/matching/` — matching summaries and recommendation interfaces.
- `components/motion/` — reusable animation wrappers and presets.
- `features/admin/` — admin screens.
- `features/matchmaker/` — Nadeem's workspace.
- `features/customer/` — customer screens.
- `features/public/` — public website.
- `i18n/` — translations and direction handling.
- `data/` — centralized mock data.
- `types/` — shared TypeScript types.
- `utils/` — formatting, unit conversion, filtering, and validation.

This is a suggested structure, not an instruction to create unnecessary folders.

Use reusable components rather than duplicating entire layouts.

## 12.2 Routing

